---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const careerStart = new Date(2012, 8, 1);
const now = new Date();

const yearsExperience = now.getFullYear() - careerStart.getFullYear() - (now.getMonth() < careerStart.getMonth() ? 1 : 0);
---

<BaseLayout title="About Me" description="Learn more about Emma Lane - Senior Software Engineer & Team Lead">
  <div class="about-page">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <img
        src="/images/real-profile-pic.jpg"
        alt="Emma Lane"
        class="about-hero__image"
      />

      <div class="pressed-hero-flower pressed-hero-flower--bloom" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/images/flowers/pressed-bloom.svg" alt="" />
      </div>

      <div class="about-hero__copy">
        <p class="home-kicker">About me</p>
        <h1>Hello hello! I'm Emma.</h1>
        <p>
          I'm a Senior Software Engineer and Team Lead with over {yearsExperience} years of experience across different technologies, projects, and domains.
          I thrive in start-up and scale-up environments, bringing strong technical expertise and leadership to every project.
        </p>
        <p>
          Spark Lane is my digital garden, where I share my journey through code, leadership, creative pursuits and continuous learning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about-content-grid">
      <aside class="about-card about-card--side">
        <p class="home-card__eyebrow">Beyond code</p>
        <h2>Curiosity tends to spill over.</h2>
        <p>When I'm not coding, you'll find me exploring creative pursuits, experimenting in the kitchen, working on my latest garden project or diving into gaming worlds. I feel that diverse interests fuel creativity and bring fresh perspectives to technical problem-solving.</p>
      </aside>
      
      <section class="about-card about-card--main">
        <!-- Right Column - Tab Navigation and Content -->
        <div class="about-me-container">
          <nav class="about-tabs" aria-label="Tabs">
            <button 
              onclick="showTab('philosophy')" 
              id="philosophy-btn"
              class="tab-btn active"
            >
              Approach & Philosophy
            </button>
            <button 
              onclick="showTab('space')" 
              id="space-btn"
              class="tab-btn"
            >
              This Space
            </button>
            <button 
              onclick="showTab('technical')" 
              id="technical-btn"
              class="tab-btn"
            >
              Technical Expertise
            </button>
            <button 
              onclick="showTab('experience')" 
              id="experience-btn"
              class="tab-btn"
            >
              Professional Experience
            </button>
          </nav>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Tab Content -->
        <div class="about-tab-panel">
          <!-- Approach & Philosophy Tab -->
          <div id="philosophy-content" class="tab-content">
            <p>
              I believe in writing clean, maintainable code and creating user experiences that are both functional and delightful. I approach development with an emphasis on accessibility first, continuous learning, community engagement, and user-centred design. By prioritising these principles, I aim to build inclusive experiences that work for everyone, foster a culture of continuous improvement, and contribute to the advancement of the tech industry as a whole.
            </p> 
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Accessibility First</strong>: Building inclusive experiences that work for everyone</li>
              <li><strong>Continuous Learning</strong>: Staying curious and embracing new technologies</li>
              <li><strong>Community Engagement</strong>: Contributing to open source and sharing knowledge</li>
              <li><strong>User-Centred Design</strong>: Putting people at the heart of technical decisions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- This Space Tab -->
          <div id="space-content" class="tab-content hidden">
            <p>Spark Lane is where I keep the different parts of my work and interests in one place. It is part professional portfolio, part blog, and part digital garden for the things I am learning, making and enjoying. Here you'll find:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Blog Posts</strong>: Technical posts, accessibility thoughts, development notes, dissertation updates and the odd personal musing</li>
              <li><strong>Portfolio</strong>: Selected projects that show how I approach software engineering, problem-solving, accessibility and user-centred design</li>
              <li><strong>Dissertation Hub</strong>: My MSc Deepfake Defence project and all related dissertation writing in one place</li>
              <li><strong>Digital Garden</strong>: Recipes, reading notes, music recommendations, watch lists and cosy gaming references</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Technical Expertise Tab -->
          <div id="technical-content" class="tab-content hidden">
            <p>I work with a diverse and modern tech stack, CI/CD and with a deep expertise in a multitude of technologies:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Backend</strong>: C#, .NET & .NET Core, ASP.NET, NodeJS, NestJS, Python, Java</li>
              <li><strong>Frontend</strong>: React, VueJS, NextJS, AngularJS, TypeScript as well as various CSS frameworks</li>
              <li><strong>CMS</strong>: Umbraco, WordPress, Contentful</li>
              <li><strong>Databases</strong>: MS SQL, MySQL, PostgreSQL, NoSQL (12 years of SQL experience)</li>              
              <li><strong>Cloud & DevOps</strong>: Azure DevOps, Azure Web Apps, Azure Functions, Docker</li>
              <li><strong>Testing</strong>: Jest, Cypress, Selenium, Playwright</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Professional Experience Tab -->
          <div id="experience-content" class="tab-content hidden">
            <p>With extensive experience across the entire software lifecycle, I've successfully designed, developed and deployed numerous desktop and web-based applications while working with and managing mixed-discipline teams. </p>
            <p>My career spans from apprentice to junior developer to team leadership, with key roles including: Team Lead, Senior Software Engineer and Lead Back-end Developer.</p>
            <p>Throughout my career, I have worked across multiple industries, from fintech to digital agencies to defense, and have delivered projects of varying sizes and complexity while developing strong leadership and technical expertise.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    
    <script is:inline>
      function showTab(tabName) {
        // Hide all content immediately
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(content => {
          content.classList.add('hidden');
          content.classList.remove('tab-fade-in');
        });
        
        // Remove active class from all buttons
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(btn => {
          btn.classList.remove('active');
        });
        
        // Show selected content with fade animation
        const selectedContent = document.getElementById(tabName + '-content');
        selectedContent.classList.remove('hidden');
        selectedContent.classList.add('tab-fade-in');
        
        // Add active class to clicked button
        const activeBtn = document.getElementById(tabName + '-btn');
        activeBtn.classList.add('active');
        
        // Reset scale after animation
        setTimeout(() => {
          activeBtn.style.transform = 'scale(1)';
        }, 200);
      }
    </script>

    <section class="about-card about-connect-card">
      <p class="home-card__eyebrow">Let's connect</p>
      <h2>Have a project in mind?</h2>
      <p>I'm always excited to connect with my peers. Whether you're interested in collaboration, have a project in mind, or want to discuss leadership and technical challenges, I'd love to hear from you.</p>
      <p>Feel free to reach out!</p>

      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmalouiselane/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="about-contact-card">
        <span class="about-card__cta">LinkedIn</span>
      </a>
      <a href="mailto:emma@sparklane.dev" class="about-contact-card">
        <span class="about-card__cta">Email me</span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>





